IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc2-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc2-factors`
IMPORT `ssc2-maternity`

-- Tests for ssc2-maternity.l4 (ss 35, 35A, 35B). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- Money figures other than the 30-pound threshold of s 35(6A) are INVENTED test inputs.
-- Calendar facts used by hand: Sunday 6 April 2025; so Sundays 30 March, 13 April, 11 May, 18 May, 1 June,
-- 8 June, 15 June, 22 June, 29 June, 6 July 2025; Sunday 31 March 2024; Sunday 28 December 2025.
-- The expected week of confinement used throughout is Sunday 15 June to Saturday 21 June 2025:
-- the 11th week before it begins on Sunday 30 March 2025 (77 days earlier); the fifth week before it ends
-- on Saturday 17 May; the fourth week before it begins on Sunday 18 May; the 66 weeks before it run from
-- Sunday 10 March 2024 to Saturday 14 June 2025.

§ `Tests -- fixtures`

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 35 test period from` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS a, `the last day` IS b

GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER, living IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Labour
`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` MEANS Labour WITH
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS weeks
    `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS living
    `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS Date 10 5 2025

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 35 test tax year beginning in` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS y

`s 35 test expected week` MEANS `s 35 test period from` (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025)

§ `Tests -- the Kleene helpers`

#ASSERT `s 35 not` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35 not` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 not` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35 both` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 both` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35 both` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35 both` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35 either` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 either` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 either` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35 either` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 122(1) weeks: Sunday to Saturday`

#ASSERT `s 35(1) the week of Part II containing the day` (Date 18 6 2025) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the week of Part II containing the day` (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the week of Part II containing the day` (Date 21 6 2025) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 15 6 2025) (Date 21 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the week of Part II containing the day` (Date 22 6 2025) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 22 6 2025) (Date 28 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the week of Part II containing the day` (Date 14 6 2025) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 8 6 2025) (Date 14 6 2025)

§ `Tests -- s 35(1)(a): the 11th week before the expected week`

#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` `s 35 test expected week` EQUALS Date 30 3 2025
-- pregnant, and on the commencement itself she has reached it
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` TRUE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 30 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` TRUE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 29 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- confined before reaching it: confined on 20 March, asked on 29 March
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` TRUE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 29 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a confinement on the day asked also counts as having been confined
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` TRUE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 29 3 2025) (JUST (Date 29 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- confinement still to come is not yet "been confined"
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` TRUE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 29 3 2025) (JUST (Date 30 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` FALSE `s 35 test expected week` (Date 1 5 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 35(1)(b), (c): the 66 weeks and the earnings`

#ASSERT `s 35(1)(b) the 66 weeks immediately preceding the expected week of confinement` `s 35 test expected week` EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 10 3 2024) (Date 14 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(b) the woman has been engaged in employment for any part of the week in the case of at least 26 of the 66 weeks` 26 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(b) the woman has been engaged in employment for any part of the week in the case of at least 26 of the 66 weeks` 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(b) the woman has been engaged in employment for any part of the week in the case of at least 26 of the 66 weeks` 66 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the tax year in which the beginning of the 66 weeks falls: 10 March 2024 is in 2023-24
#ASSERT (`s 35(1)(c) the tax year in which the beginning of the period of 66 weeks falls` `s 35 test expected week`)'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2023
-- expected week from Sunday 6 July 2025: 66 weeks begin Sunday 31 March 2024, still 2023-24
#ASSERT (`s 35(1)(c) the tax year in which the beginning of the period of 66 weeks falls` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 6 7 2025) (Date 12 7 2025)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2023
-- expected week from Sunday 13 July 2025: 66 weeks begin Sunday 7 April 2024, which is in 2024-25
#ASSERT (`s 35(1)(c) the tax year in which the beginning of the period of 66 weeks falls` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 13 7 2025) (Date 19 7 2025)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
-- expected week from Sunday 12 July 2026: 66 weeks begin on Sunday 6 April 2025 itself, the first day of 2025-26
#ASSERT (`s 35(1)(c) the tax year in which the beginning of the period of 66 weeks falls` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 12 7 2026) (Date 18 7 2026)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT (`s 35(1)(c) the tax year in which the beginning of the period of 66 weeks falls` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 5 7 2026) (Date 11 7 2026)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024

-- (6A), (6B): 30 pounds, or the amount an order specifies for a tax year after 2001-2002
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the amount specified in subsection (6A) in pounds` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) NOTHING EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) (JUST 40) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2002) (JUST 40) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2001) (JUST 40) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 35(6A) the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 1999) (JUST 40) EQUALS 30
-- (1)(c) earnings not less than the threshold (equal counts); unknown earnings are not covered
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(c) her average weekly earnings are not less than the maternity allowance threshold` (JUST 30) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(c) her average weekly earnings are not less than the maternity allowance threshold` (JUST 29) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(c) her average weekly earnings are not less than the maternity allowance threshold` (JUST 31) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(c) her average weekly earnings are not less than the maternity allowance threshold` NOTHING 30 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 35(1)(d) and the whole of s 35(1)`

#ASSERT `s 35(1)(d) she is not entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(d) she is not entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1)(d) she is not entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: (a), (b), (c), (d)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 35(2), (3A), (3E): the period, its reduction, and the week excluded`

#ASSERT `s 35(2) the maternity allowance period` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)
-- 30 March to 27 December 2025 is 273 days, 39 weeks
#ASSERT `s 35(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity allowance period is reduced` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `s 35(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity allowance period is reduced` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST 26) EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 35(3A) the maternity allowance period as reduced` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST 26) EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 9 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(3A) the maternity allowance period as reduced` (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS `s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(3E) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance for the week` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(3E) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance for the week` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(3E) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance for the week` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 35(4): death of the woman`

-- the period is Sunday 30 March to Saturday 27 December 2025; arguments: first day of the week, the period, the day of death
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 15 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- death before the period begins
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 6 4 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 29 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- death on Wednesday 11 June: the week of death is 8 to 14 June; the following week is excluded, that week and earlier ones are not
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 15 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 11 6 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 8 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 11 6 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 1 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 11 6 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- death on Saturday 14 June (last day of its week) and on Sunday 15 June (first day of the next)
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 15 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 14 6 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 15 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 15 6 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 22 6 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 15 6 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- death on the first and the last day of the period
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 6 4 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 30 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 28 12 2025) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 27 12 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- death after the period: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 35(4) the allowance is payable for the week` (Date 4 1 2026) (`s 35 test period from` (Date 30 3 2025) (Date 27 12 2025)) (JUST (Date 28 12 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 35(5), (6): the daily rate and confinement`

#ASSERT `s 35(5) the amount payable by way of maternity allowance for a day` 70 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 35(5) the amount payable by way of maternity allowance for a day` 0 EQUALS 0
-- (a) a living child, whatever the weeks; (b) 24 completed weeks or more, whether alive or dead
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the woman is confined by the labour` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 20 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the woman is confined by the labour` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 24 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the woman is confined by the labour` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 23 FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the woman is confined by the labour` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 30 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the day on which the woman is confined` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 30 TRUE) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 5 2025)
#ASSERT `s 35(6) the day on which the woman is confined` (`s 35(6) test labour beginning at weeks with the child living` 23 FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 35(6B), (6C), (6D), (7)`

#ASSERT `s 35(6B) an order may increase the amount for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2002) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(6B) an order may increase the amount for the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2001) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(6C) the Secretary of State is required to have regard to the movement in prices` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(6C) the Secretary of State is required to have regard to the movement in prices` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(6D) the Secretary of State is required to review the amount in the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(7) the court may take into consideration that the mother is being paid maternity allowance` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(7) the court may take into consideration that the mother is being paid maternity allowance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- the permission of (6B): used in a year after 2001-2002 the Secretary of State may increase the amount
#TRACE `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State may increase the amount by order` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 35(6B) increase the amount specified in subsection (6A) by order` AT 10
-- a year before the power applies leaves nothing to do
#EVAL `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State may increase the amount by order` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2001)
-- the duty of (6C) arises only while deciding
#TRACE `s 35(6C) the Secretary of State must have regard to the movement in prices` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 35(6C) have regard to the movement in the general level of prices` AT 3
#EVAL `s 35(6C) the Secretary of State must have regard to the movement in prices` FALSE
-- the review of (6D): 2025-26 starts on 6 April 2025 and ends on 5 April 2026, 364 days later
#TRACE `s 35(6D) the Secretary of State must review the amount in the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 35(6D) carry out such a review of the amount for the time being specified in subsection (6A) as he thinks fit` AT 364
#TRACE `s 35(6D) the Secretary of State must review the amount in the tax year` (`s 35 test tax year beginning in` 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 35(6B) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 35(6D) carry out such a review of the amount for the time being specified in subsection (6A) as he thinks fit` AT 365
-- the prohibition of (7): a court that takes the payment into consideration is in breach
#TRACE `s 35(7) a court may not take the mother's payment into consideration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 35(7) any court` DOES `s 35(7) take into consideration that the mother of the child is being paid maternity allowance` AT 5

§ `Tests -- s 35A(4), (5), (5B), (1)`

#ASSERT `s 35A(4) the woman's average weekly earnings in pounds` (JUST 120) EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `s 35A(4) the woman's average weekly earnings in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(c): arguments: regulations so provide, self-employed, paid Class 2, could have paid, prescribed rate, last day of the week, order amount
-- (i) paid: 90 per cent of the payment is the prescribed rate, so the payment is 100 when the rate is 90
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 100
-- (ii) could have paid but did not: the threshold in force on the last day of the week
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 40
-- the order amount is not used for a tax year that is not after 2001-2002: week ending 5 April 2002 is in 2001-02
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 90 (Date 5 4 2002) (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 90 (Date 6 4 2002) (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 40
-- neither paid nor able to pay; no regulations; not self-employed
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35A(5)(c) the payment that the woman is treated as having received in respect of the week` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 90 (Date 14 6 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35A(5B) subsection (5B) applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35A(5B) subsection (5B) applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): arguments: (5B) applies, average weekly earnings, the prescribed weekly rate (180 is invented)
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) 180 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 180 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` NOTHING (JUST 100) 180 EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` NOTHING (JUST 250) 180 EQUALS JUST 180
-- 90 per cent of 200 is exactly 180, the prescribed rate
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` NOTHING (JUST 200) 180 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` NOTHING NOTHING 180 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 100) 180 EQUALS JUST 90

